course: dictionary
lesson: 8209
title: Retirement: the end of working life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Retirement is a word about the end of working life. When a person retires, they stop going to work for good, usually because they are older. «At the other end of working life comes retirement, when people stop paid work for good.» The clue is "other end": work is at one end of life, and retirement is at the other.
explain: The words around retirement give more clues. «Early retirement» often means being pushed out of a job before the usual age, so the word "pushed" tells you it was not the person's choice. A «retirement community» is a housing estate built for old people.
explain: Retirement can also mean that a sports player stops playing. Check which meaning fits by swapping in a simple phrase such as "stopped working" or "stopped playing" and reading the sentence again.
fact: Retirement is a noun. Its plural is retirements.
fact: Retirement means the time when a person stops working for good, usually because they are older.
fact: «Golden years» means old age, the years after retirement.
fact: In retirement, many people get a pension and enjoy hobbies or time with grandchildren.
fact: In sport, retirement means a player stops playing.
exercise: «At the other end of working life comes retirement, when people stop paid work for good.» What is retirement? | The time when a person starts their first job | A holiday from school | *The time when a person stops working for good | A party for new workers
exercise: «Early retirement» often means what? | Going to school early | *Being pushed out of a job before the usual age | Working extra hours on a Sunday | Starting work at a very young age
exercise: «The golden years» means which of these? | Early mornings before school | Gold coins saved in a bank | *Old age, the years after retirement | The sunniest days of summer
test: Maya says retirement is a holiday from school. Why is she wrong? | Retirement is a kind of school trip | *Retirement is about stopping paid work for good, usually because of age | Retirement means learning new words | Retirement is about school being too hard
test: «A retirement community is a housing estate built for old people.» What kind of place is it? | *A housing estate built for old people | A sports stadium | A shop full of gold | A school for children
exam: Which sentence uses retirement in the sports sense? | *After twenty years, the striker announced his retirement from football | Early retirement often means being pushed out of a job | Grandma spends her retirement with her grandchildren | At the other end of working life comes retirement
